| `dependency_audit.accepted.<app>` | object | `{}` in a project whose `frontend_stack` is not `astro`; otherwise the one `astro` row below | a frontend app's directory name under `layers.frontend.root` (one path part) mapped to at least one advisory row; `{}` accepts nothing | `scripts/audit_dependencies.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `dependency_audit.accepted` row | Lists an app's accepted advisories, each judged on every `make fe-audit`. A row whose app is not one the run audits fails as stale; an app with no advisory under it is refused with exit 14. Absent, the audit writes `[using default] dependency_audit.accepted = {}` to stderr. | fixing the package: the app's `package.json` and `package-lock.json` | always |
